        			</td>
        			<td style="vertical-align:top; width:62.75pt">
        			<p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">$5,500</span></span></span></span></p>
        			</td>
        		</tr>
        	</tbody>
        </table>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">25% of personnel costs for any community parade</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="4" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">75% of personnel costs for all other events</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">any park reservation fees associated with a special event.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The fees and costs shall be estimated in writing by the issuing authority and given to the applicant prior to the issuance of the special event permit.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The fees and costs shall be paid by the applicant to the City within thirty days from the receipt of the bill for such costs and fees.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">When a special event permit is sought for an expressive activity involving a demonstration, rally or march, as defined by this chapter, and the special event will not require temporary street closures, cost recovery shall be limited to the administrative processing fee.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">When a special event permit is sought for an expressive activity requiring street closure or other City services, personnel and equipment, the special event permit may be conditioned upon payment of estimated costs incurred by the City to a maximum amount of five hundred dollars. </span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">In no way will an indigent applicant&rsquo;s First Amendment rights be impaired in any fashion.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The terms and conditions of a permit shall not infringe upon the rights of petition, assembly or free expression protected by the First Amendment of the U.S. Constitution and/or Article 1, Section 3, 4 and 5 of the Washington State Constitution. </span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 6, 2022</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, July 22, 2022</p><p>ORD C36203 Section 9</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.39.100">Section 10.39.100</a> Authorized Special Event Vendors<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The issuance of a special event permit confers upon the permit holder the right to control and regulate the sale of goods, food and/or beverages within the special event venue in accordance with the terms and conditions of the special event permit.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.39.110">Section 10.39.110</a> Responsibility<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">This chapter does not create any duty owed by the City of Spokane to any specific person, party or class. Any duty nonetheless deemed to exist or arise in connection with the City&rsquo;s permitting function shall be deemed a duty to the general public as a whole and not to any specific person, party or class.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>						<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=10.40">Chapter 10.40</a> Itinerant Vendors</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.40.010">Section 10.40.010</a> Itinerant Vendor Designation & Permit - When Required<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A regular or temporary business issued a registration under chapter&nbsp;</span><a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline" target="_blank"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">8.01 SMC</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;must obtain a separate &ldquo;itinerant vendor&rdquo; permit from the City of Spokane Office of Taxes and Licenses under any of the following circumstances:</span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Where the person is engaged in the business of selling or delivering goods or services within the City from a fixed or temporary location as an itinerant vendor, except mobile food vendors&nbsp;shall not be considered itinerant vendors.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Examples are people selling prepackaged food that requires refrigeration or wares from roving vehicles in the streets, except mobile food vendors. (Cross Reference:&nbsp;</span><a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.01.220" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline" target="_blank"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC 8.01.220</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">).</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Where the person travels from door to door as the principal means of conducting business, offering, exposing for sale, or selling within the City any goods, merchandise, service, or product.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Where the person engages in any business in the City with no permanent location. (Cross Reference:&nbsp;</span><a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.01.070" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline" target="_blank"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC 8.01.070</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">).</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A person who engages in constitutionally protected expressive activities in the public right-of-way shall not be required to obtain a business registration unless the person engages in business activities. Constitutionally protected expressive activities conducted in the public right-of-way shall include, but is not limited to, street performers. For the purposes of this section, a street performer means an individual, including street musicians, who performs any form of artistic expression. The voluntary contribution of money or other items of value by members of the public to the individual in association with the expressive activity shall not result in the requirement of obtaining a business registration. A person who engages in constitutionally protected expressive activities in the public right-of-way must still comply with all other regulations regarding conduct in the public right-of-way.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 4, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, June 10, 2026</p><p>ORD C36863 Section 3</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.40.020">Section 10.40.020</a> REPEALED (Itinerant Vendor Permit Required)<br />
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 31, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36652 Section 16</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.40.025">Section 10.40.025</a> Violation<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">If a person engages in activities defined in&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=10.40.010" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC 10.40.010</span></span></a><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&nbsp;without a current itinerant vendor permit issued by the City of Spokane Taxes and Licensing Office, they are subject to a penalty.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A violation of this chapter is a civil infraction. Each day upon which a violation occurs or is knowingly continued constitutes a separate violation.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Itinerant vendors must comply with all state and local laws.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 14, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, August 24, 2025</p><p>ORD C36702 Section 19</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.40.030">Section 10.40.030</a> Application<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Persons within the definition of <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=10.40.010"><span style="color:blue">SMC 10.40.010</span></a> must further truthfully disclose on their business registration application the following information:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Applicant&rsquo;s permanent address.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Address of his principal(s) and supplier(s).</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Address of the fixed location within the City of Spokane, if any, from which the activity is to be conducted.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Nature and type of goods or services to be sold and that the applicant has all necessary licenses, registrations, or permits from owners of copyright, trademark or other such lawful interests in the goods or materials to be sold; and</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Applicant has not violated the City license code, registration code, or the copyright or trademark laws of the United States or had his application for a City license or registration denied within the past twelve months.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The license officer may require proper documentation of the application as he deems necessary prior to issuing the license or as a condition of not revoking or suspending the license after issuance.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">All applications shall be filed at least three business days before issuance.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 8, 2012</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, October 15, 2012</p><p>ORD C34926 Section 24</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.40.040">Section 10.40.040</a> REPEALED (Expiration)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C33824.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.40.050">Section 10.40.050</a> Limitations on Location<br />
        <p>The licensing officer does not issue a license or registration with an “itinerant vendor” permit for activity upon park property, except by prior permission of the park board.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 8, 2012</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, October 15, 2012</p><p>ORD C34926 Section 25</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.40.060">Section 10.40.060</a> Regulations<br />
        <p>Subject to specification by the license officer in the license, every person within the definition of <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=10.40.010">SMC 10.40.010</a> is required to: </p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>refrain from using excessively noisy devices or methods to attract public attention to his wares or services and from shouting or calling his wares or services in a loud or boisterous manner;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>keep all conveyances and containers for foodstuffs and edibles clean and sanitary and to keep all consumables well covered and protected from all dirt, insects or other contamination;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>refrain from standing, by person or vehicle, upon any public way more than ten minutes in any one place;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>move from a location adjacent to another’s place of business or residence when requested by someone in charge of such business or residence;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>move from a location included within the boundaries of a special event when requested by the chief of police or someone in charge of such special event;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>refrain from any illegal, fraudulent or deceptive practice;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>have upon his person for display upon inquiry by any person a copy of the City license and, in addition, documents showing he is authorized by the copyright or trademark owner to sell the goods concerned.</li></ol>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>						<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=10.41A">Chapter 10.41A</a> Special Police Officers</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.41A.010">Section 10.41A.010</a> In General<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">This chapter specifies the general administrative procedures of <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=08.01">chapter 08.01</a> SMC&nbsp;and provides substantive regulations of special police officers.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Special or private police officers under this chapter differ from private detectives and security guards licensed under chapter 18.165 RCW and chapter 18.170 RCW in that they have a police commission and they differ from members of the police reserve force.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 31, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36652 Section 18</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.41A.020">Section 10.41A.020</a> Purpose<br />
        <p>The purpose of this chapter is to assist the police department in carrying out its law enforcement responsibilities by conferring upon persons certain law enforcement authority in limited and specific instances.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.41A.030">Section 10.41A.030</a> Definitions<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>“Applicant” is the person employing the individual for whom a special police commission is sought.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>“Special police officer” or “private police officer” is an individual employed by someone other than the City police department for security purposes having a commission from the chief of police to exercise the powers of a law enforcement officer limited to the scope of his employment and the terms of his commission.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>The “subject” of an application is the individual for whom the commission is sought.</li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.41A.040">Section 10.41A.040</a> License Required<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">No person may act or pretend to act as a special police officer without a current valid commission.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">No person may employ an individual as a special police officer unless the individual has a current valid commission.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The license required for a special police officer is in the form of a commission from the chief of police and is a license as provided in <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=08.01">chapter 08.01</a> SMC.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 31, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36652 Section 19</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.41A.050">Section 10.41A.050</a> Application<br />
        <p>The applicant is required to set forth in the application: </p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>the name and address of the applicant;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>the address or other description of the location(s) where the subject will be employed;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>the full name, date of birth and address of the subject;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>all facts known to the applicant regarding the subject’s qualifications under <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=10.41A.060">SMC 10.41A.060</a>;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>the reason why the applicant believes the subject should be commissioned; and<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>a description of the proposed responsibilities and functions of the subject and of the subject’s present scope of employment.</li></ol>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.41A.060">Section 10.41A.060</a> Qualifications<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">To be eligible for a commission a subject, at the time of application, must:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">be at least twenty-one years of age;</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">be a citizen of the United States;</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">have a high school diploma or equivalent;</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">be of good moral character;</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">not have been convicted of a:</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">felony,</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">crime of moral turpitude, or</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">crime involving a controlled substance;</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="6">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">not have been involuntarily committed to an institution or treatment program for:</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">a mental disorder, or</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">alcohol or controlled substance abuse;</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="7">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">have at least ninety days&rsquo; experience in security affairs in the applicant&rsquo;s employ.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">This qualification may be waived by the chief if the subject:</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol>
        			<li style="list-style-type:none">
        			<ol style="list-style-type:lower-roman">
        				<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">is employed by the applicant and the chief determines that the subject has had ninety days&rsquo; experience in security affairs with a previous employer, or</span></span></span></li>
        			</ol>
        			</li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol>
        			<li style="list-style-type:none">
        			<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-roman">
        				<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">has completed the training in subsection (B) of this section.</span></span></span></li>
        			</ol>
        			</li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">In addition to subsection (A) of this section, before receiving a commission a subject must:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">satisfactorily complete a training program specified by the chief of police, and</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">make an oath to uphold the constitution and laws of the United States and of the State of Washington and the Charter and ordinances of the City of Spokane.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.41A.070">Section 10.41A.070</a> Special Regulations<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>No special police officer, while on duty as such, may carry any firearm or dangerous weapon unless his commission specifically authorizes him to do so.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>The chief issues identification insignia to each special police officer. An officer is required to carry that identification on his person at all times when on duty and to display it when called upon to identify himself.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>A special police officer may wear such badge and uniform only as have been approved by the chief.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>A special police officer may use a motor vehicle with special marking, insignia, lights or equipment only with the prior approval of the chief.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>While performing the duties of employment, a special police officer is required to conform with the standards of conduct prescribed for police officers and may not do any act which would be unlawful if committed by a law enforcement officer.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>The chief may require a special police officer to undergo additional training whenever appropriate.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Every special police officer must comply with such rules and regulations regarding licensing, training, conduct and other matters as the chief may from time to time issue.</li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.41A.080">Section 10.41A.080</a> Termination<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A special police commission expires after one year.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An expired commission may be renewed upon application.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A special police commission terminates upon termination of the officer&rsquo;s employment by the applicant.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The applicant must immediately notify the chief of an officer&rsquo;s termination of employment.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The chief may suspend or revoke a commission at any time because of violation of the provisions of this code or for other cause.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Upon expiration, termination, suspension or revocation of his commission the officer must immediately surrender to the applicant his identification and any badge, uniform and other property connected with his office.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.41A.090">Section 10.41A.090</a> Penalties<br />
        <p>When the chief finds that a special police officer has violated a term of this code, in lieu of or as a condition of suspension or revocation of the commission, the chief may issue a notice of civil infraction and may require the officer to make restitution to any person damaged by the violation.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.41A.100">Section 10.41A.100</a> Responsibility of Applicant<br />
        <p>The conferral of a special police commission does not affect the employer/employee relationship between the applicant and the officer. The employer remains responsible for the acts of the officer within the scope of employment until the applicant notifies the chief of termination of employment as required by <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=10.41A.080">SMC 10.41A.080(B)</a>.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>						<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=10.42">Chapter 10.42</a> REPEALED (Solicitation)</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.42.010">Section 10.42.010</a> REPEALED (“Charitable Purpose” Defined)<br />
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Wednesday, September 2, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, October 8, 2026</p><p>ORD C36923 Section 2</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.42.020">Section 10.42.020</a> REPEALED (“Solicit” Defined)<br />
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Wednesday, September 2, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, October 8, 2026</p><p>ORD C36923 Section 2</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.42.030">Section 10.42.030</a> REPEALED (Charitable Solicitation Permit Required)<br />
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Wednesday, September 2, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, October 8, 2026</p><p>ORD C36923 Section 2</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.42.040">Section 10.42.040</a> REPEALED (Charitable Solicitation Application)<br />
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Wednesday, September 2, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, October 8, 2026</p><p>ORD C36923 Section 2</p>						<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=10.43">Chapter 10.43</a> Telephone and Telegraph Construction</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.43.010">Section 10.43.010</a> Construction Permit Required<br />
        <p>No telegraph, telephone, or other communication utility, whether operating under a City franchise or under federal or state authority, may construct or install any lines or other equipment within a public right-of-way without a specific permit for each project, issued by the department of engineering services, in addition to a street obstruction permit as provided in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17G.010.210">SMC 17G.010.210(D)</a>.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.43.020">Section 10.43.020</a> Application<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A communication utility must file with the director of engineering services a written application for a construction permit, accompanied by detailed maps, plans and specifications showing:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">all excavations;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the apparatus and appliances proposed;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the location of poles, wires, cables, conduits, pipes, manholes and other apparatus;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the duct, conduit or portion of the system of poles or masts reserved for the exclusive use of the City;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the structure of all apparatus and appliances; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="6">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the height above or depth below the finished grade of the public way.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The utility must also:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">file the application,</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">pay the fee, and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">post the bond</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:40px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">for a street obstruction permit.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.43.030">Section 10.43.030</a> Location of Equipment<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>At all times, subject to the direction of the director of engineering services, the utility must locate its poles, conduits, pipes, manholes and other appliances so as to not unreasonably interfere with existing public or private utility facilities or trees, shrubbery or improvements on abutting property.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>In the downtown area and in other areas where utilities are, or are expected to be, underground, the director may require communication facilities to be installed underground.</li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.43.040">Section 10.43.040</a> Performance of Work<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>At all times, subject to the direction of the director of engineering services, the utility must perform the work of construction, installation and maintenance within public ways with diligence but with minimum interference with public travel, access to abutting properties and existing utility services.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Unless approved by the director, no utility may excavate more than one block at a time.</li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.43.050">Section 10.43.050</a> Relocation of Facilities<br />
        <p>A permit under this chapter does not confer upon any communication utility any vested right in the continued presence of any communication facilities in a public way. The director of engineering services may require a utility to relocate, at the utility’s expense, any apparatus or appliances when necessary to conform to a change in grade or alteration of the location of any other utility required by the City.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.43.060">Section 10.43.060</a> Indemnification<br />
        <p>As may be specified in any franchise or the required street obstruction permit and bond, any utility obtaining a permit under this chapter agrees to indemnify and hold harmless the City from all claims and costs resulting from the installation, construction and maintenance of communication lines or equipment in a public way, including without limitation the failure of the permittee hereunder to promptly and adequately restore to its original condition any excavated portion of a public way.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 11, 2007</p><p>ORD C34041 Section 1 (Recodification)</p>						<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=10.45">Chapter 10.45</a> Used Goods</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.45.010">Section 10.45.010</a> REPEALED (Purpose)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35611</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, April 16, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, May 23, 2018</p><p>ORD C35611 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.45.020">Section 10.45.020</a> Definitions<br />
        <ol type="A">
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			&ldquo;Used goods&rdquo; means all items of tangible personal property except:</p>
        		<ol>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					motor vehicles required to be registered under Title 46 RCW;&nbsp;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					junk material, such as aluminum cans, paper and scrap lumber and nonprecious metal, which is intended for recycling or remanufacture;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					containers, such as glass bottles, intended for recycling and reuse;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					used metal construction or fabrication materials, such as pipe, channels, angles or beams; which property is bought, sold, exchanged, pledged, consigned or transferred at any time after its original retail sale; and</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					Products, such as machinery or machinery parts, which have been remanufactured or restored in whole or in part and which are sold in retail stores.</p>
        			</li>
        		</ol>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			&ldquo;Yard sale&rdquo; means a public offering for sale of clothing, furniture, toys and other used goods, including without limitation personal and household items, at a residence located within an area zoned residential single-family (RSF), residential single-family compact (RSF-C), or residential two-family (RTF). For purposes of this chapter, &ldquo;garage sales&rdquo;, &ldquo;rummage sales,&rdquo; and all other similar commonly-used terms are equivalent to &ldquo;garage sale&rdquo;.</p>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, April 16, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, May 23, 2018</p><p>ORD C35611 Section 2</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.45.030">Section 10.45.030</a> REPEALED (“Dealer in Used Goods” Defined)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35611<o:p></o:p></p>
        <p>
        	&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, April 16, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, May 23, 2018</p><p>ORD C35611 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.45.040">Section 10.45.040</a> REPEALED (License Required)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35611<o:p></o:p></p>
        <p>
        	&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, April 16, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, May 23, 2018</p><p>ORD C35611 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.45.050">Section 10.45.050</a> REPEALED (Records Required)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35611<o:p></o:p></p>
        <p>
        	&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, April 16, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, May 23, 2018</p><p>ORD C35611 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.45.060">Section 10.45.060</a> REPEALED (Special Regulations)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35611<o:p></o:p></p>
        <p>
        	&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, April 16, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, May 23, 2018</p><p>ORD C35611 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.45.070">Section 10.45.070</a> Prohibited Acts: Penalty<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">It is a violation of this chapter to conduct four (4) or more yard sales as defined in this chapter in a calendar year or to conduct a yard sale at a single location for longer than three (3) days.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A violation of this section is a civil infraction. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 14, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, August 24, 2025</p><p>ORD C36702 Section 20</p>						<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=10.46">Chapter 10.46</a> REPEALED (Weights and Measures)</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.46.010">Section 10.46.010</a> REPEALED (In General)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34969.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 25, 2013</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, May 3, 2013</p><p>ORD C34969 Section 9</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.46.020">Section 10.46.020</a> REPEALED (Standard Systems of Weights and Measures)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34969.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 25, 2013</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, May 3, 2013</p><p>ORD C34969 Section 10</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.46.030">Section 10.46.030</a> REPEALED (Official City Standards)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34969.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 25, 2013</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, May 3, 2013</p><p>ORD C34969 Section 11</p></form>
        </div>
        </div></td>
        	</tr>
        </table>
